          %h2#categorical_semantics Categorical semantics
          %p
            We discuss the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of h-propositions.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} locally cartesian closed category
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics+of+homotopy+type+theory"} sufficient structure
            to interpret all the above type theory. This means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+system"} weak factorization system
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+path+objects"} stable path objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+cofibrations"} trivial cofibrations
            are preserved by pullback along fibrations between fibrant objects. (We ignore questions of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence"} coherence
          %p
            Then for a fibrant object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi isProp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isProp(A)
            defined above (with the first definition) is obtained by taking
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            of the path-object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^I \to A\times A
            along the projection
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\times A\to 1
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global element
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi isProp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isProp(A)
            is therefore equivalent to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of the path-object, which exactly means a (right)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            between the two projections
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\times A\;\rightrightarrows\; A
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                any two maps
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\;\rightrightarrows\; A
                are homotopic
          %p
            More generally, we may apply this locally. Suppose that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to B
            is a fibration, which we can regard as a dependent type
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Type
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\colon B \vdash A(x)\colon Type.
          %p Then we have a dependent type
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi isProp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\colon B \vdash isProp(A(x))\colon Type
          %p
            represented by a fibration
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi isProp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isProp(A)\to B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}/B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi isProp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isProp(A)\to B
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            exactly when any two maps in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}/B
            into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to B
            are homotopic over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi B
                  %mi isProp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{x\colon B} isProp(A(x))
          %p
            in global context, which has a global element precisely when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi isProp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isProp(A)\to B
            has a section.
